    "field_prefix": {
      "from": "droplive_",
      "to": "worldfixture_"
    },
    "reason": "the originating product's name is removed from the public contract, before anyone depends on it. It appeared in data every consumer reads: organization domains and person addresses under `.droplive.test`, the `droplive_*` field names carried inside provider API responses, the agent projection's api_version, and the composer's scheduled-arrivals seed key. Reversing this rename on the parsed JSON reproduces all 23 unmigrated reference files exactly, which is what proves no world fact moved with the name. It has to be reversed on the parsed JSON and not on the bytes: the projections are canonical JSON with sorted keys, so `droplive_person_id` sorted before `email` while `worldfixture_person_id` sorts after `name`, and the rename reorders keys as well as renaming them.",
